  "notes": "covey: Gambel's quail, a cock: plump and blue-grey, chestnut crown and flanks streaked white, a black face and throat edged white, a black patch on a buff belly, and a black teardrop plume curling forward off its head. Coveys of a dozen or more scuttle between the desert bushes in run-stop-peck, one now and then up on a bush top keeping watch. Pressed, the covey runs off on foot together, heads down; only when you are nearly on it does it burst up all at once on whirring wings, scatter low and come down a little way off.",
